# Test Case Payload Format (canonical)

Canonical JSON structure and HTML templates for a single test case. Used by draft files (`drafts/test-cases-draft.json`) and TestIT MCP `testit_create_case`. Skills **docs-to-test-cases** and **testit-plan-create** build payloads from this format.

---

## Full JSON schema (one test case)

```json
{
  "summary": "<p>...</p>",
  "preconditions": "<p>...</p>",
  "priority": 2,
  "executionType": 2,
  "customValues": {
    "ids": [],
    "createdValues": []
  },
  "steps": [
    {
      "name": "<p>Step 1</p>",
      "executionType": 0,
      "expectedResult": "<p>Step 1</p>"
    }
  ],
  "isForceUpdate": false,
  "behaviourGroups": [],
  "relatedIssues": [
    {
      "key": "PROJECT-123",
      "description": "Issue title",
      "type": "Task",
      "iconUrl": "https://..."
    }
  ]
}
```

### Field notes

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| **summary** | string (HTML) | Summary block: User Story, Product, Account type(s), Brand. Use template below. |
| **preconditions** | string (HTML) | Entry point(s), Entry point(s) for AQA, Note. Use template below. |
| **priority** | number | e.g. 1–3 (2 = normal). |
| **executionType** | number | e.g. 2 = Manual (0 = other). |
| **customValues** | object | `ids`: IDs from MCP `testit_get_fields(project_id)` — use `id` from each field's `values[]` (e.g. Keywords); `createdValues`: empty array. |
| **steps** | array | Each: `name` (HTML), `executionType` (0), `expectedResult` (HTML). |
| **isForceUpdate** | boolean | Usually false. |
| **behaviourGroups** | array | Often empty. |
| **relatedIssues** | array | At least one. `iconUrl` — always the fixed URL (see relatedIssues format below). |

---

## HTML template — Summary

Use this structure for `summary`. Replace the placeholder text after each label; keep the HTML and green styling for labels.

```html
<p><span style="color: rgb(102, 153, 102); background-color: transparent; font-weight: bolder;">User Story:&nbsp;</span><br></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span style="color: rgb(102, 153, 102);">Product:&nbsp;</span></span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span style="color: rgb(102, 153, 102);">Account type(/s):&nbsp;</span></span><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><br></span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span style="color: rgb(102, 153, 102);">Brand:&nbsp;</span></span></p>
```

**Filling:** Insert content after each green label (User Story, Product, Account type(s), Brand). Example for User Story: put the story text after `</span><br></p>` on the first line, or in a new `<p>`.

---

## HTML template — Preconditions

Use this structure for `preconditions`. Replace placeholders after labels; keep the blue styling for "Entry point(s) for AQA" and "Note".

```html
<p><span style="font-weight: bolder; background-color: transparent;"><span style="color: rgb(102, 153, 102);">Entry point(/s):&nbsp;</span></span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: bolder; background-color: transparent;"><span style="color: rgb(102, 153, 102);"><br></span></span></p>
<p><span style="color: rgb(7, 71, 166); font-weight: 700;">Entry point(/s) for AQA:&nbsp;</span><span style="font-weight: bolder; background-color: transparent;"><span style="color: rgb(102, 153, 102);"></span></span></p>
<p><br></p>
<p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="color: rgb(7, 71, 166); font-weight: 700;">Note:&nbsp;</span></p>
```

**Filling:** Add Entry points, Entry points for AQA, and Note after the corresponding labels.

---

## Steps format

Each step object:

```json
{
  "name": "<p>Action or instruction (e.g. Step 1)</p>",
  "executionType": 0,
  "expectedResult": "<p>Expected result for this step</p>"
}
```

- **name**: Short HTML paragraph (e.g. `<p>Step 1</p>` or `<p>Open the app and log in.</p>`).
- **executionType**: Use 0 (default).
- **expectedResult**: Short HTML paragraph describing the expected outcome.

---

## relatedIssues format

**relatedIssues** must always use the same format. At least one item (Jira ticket) required.

- **key** — Jira ticket id (issue key, e.g. PROJECT-123).
- **description** — Jira ticket summary (full title or short description).
- **type** — Jira ticket type (Task, Story, Bug, Epic, etc.).
- **iconUrl** — always use: `https://jira.ringcentral.com/secure/viewavatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=22485&avatarType=issuetype`

```json
{
  "key": "WEBOPS-1348",
  "description": "Express-setup: Minor release: Update production with new OCI_IMAGE_TAG",
  "type": "Task",
  "iconUrl": "https://jira.ringcentral.com/secure/viewavatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=22485&avatarType=issuetype"
}
```

